# Coach App

Standalone Cloudflare Worker (`src/workers/coach-app.js`). Deployed separately from the main platform but sharing the same D1 database. Secured via Cloudflare Access.

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    Coach[Coach\nmobile browser] --> Access[Cloudflare Access\nZero Trust policy]
    Access -->|cf-access-authenticated-user-email| Worker[egac-coach Worker]
    Worker -->|No header| Block[403 Forbidden]
    Worker -->|Valid| D1[(D1 — shared\ndatabase)]
```

## Authentication

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Coach
    participant CF as Cloudflare Access
    participant W as Coach Worker

    C->>CF: GET coach.eastgrinsteadac.co.uk
    CF->>CF: Check email policy
    CF-->>C: Auth challenge (if not logged in)
    C->>CF: Authenticate via Google / OTP
    CF->>W: Request + cf-access-authenticated-user-email header
    W->>W: Header present?
    alt Missing
        W-->>C: 403 Forbidden
    else Present
        W->>D1: Query session data
        W-->>C: Session register HTML
    end
```

> The Worker's header check is defence in depth — the primary protection is the Access policy.

## Session register

```mermaid
graph TB
    Register[Session register\n?date=YYYY-MM-DD] --> Tasters
    Register --> Members

    Tasters[TASTERS\nbookings JOIN enquiries\nWHERE session_date=? AND status=confirmed]
    Members[MEMBERS\nathletes WHERE status=active\nLEFT JOIN attendance_log]

    Tasters --> TRow[Name · Age group badge · TASTER badge\nPhone · CHECK IN button]
    Members --> MRow[Name · Age group badge\nEmergency contact · ⚕ if medical info\nCHECK IN button]
```

## Check-in logic

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Coach
    participant Worker
    participant D1

    Coach->>Worker: POST /api/checkin { id, type, date }
    alt type = taster
        Worker->>D1: SELECT checked_in_at FROM bookings
        Worker->>D1: UPDATE bookings SET checked_in_at = now()
        Worker->>D1: INSERT OR IGNORE INTO attendance_log
    else type = member
        Worker->>D1: SELECT FROM attendance_log
        Worker->>D1: INSERT OR IGNORE INTO attendance_log
        Worker->>D1: UPDATE athletes SET last_attended_at = today
    end
    Worker-->>Coach: { ok: true, checked_in: true }
```

Unchecking removes the `attendance_log` entry and clears `checked_in_at`. Past sessions' records are never modified.

## Deployment

```bash
wrangler deploy --config wrangler-coach.toml
```

Then in **Cloudflare Zero Trust** → Access → Applications → Add Self-hosted:
- Domain: `coach.eastgrinsteadac.co.uk`
- Policy: Allow → Email addresses → list each coach

